x-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="39">Absolutely, let’s weave those ideas in!</p>
<p data-start="41" data-end="118">So within PlenumHub, we could add a couple of really interesting mechanisms.</p>
<p data-start="120" data-end="636">First, a <strong data-start="129" data-end="180">Spelling and Pronunciation Error Reporting Tool</strong>. This would allow users to flag not just typos or spelling errors in text-based contributions, but also to tag pronunciation issues if there are audio components. For example, if someone uploads a spoken explanation, other users could note, “Hey, this pronunciation of a technical term isn’t clear,” or “There’s a common spelling variation here.” It’s kind of like a peer-review layer that respects the nuances of language in both written and spoken form.</p>
<p data-start="638" data-end="1252">Then, there’s the idea of a <strong data-start="666" data-end="681">Media Quine</strong>. That’s a really neat concept! Essentially, the platform could detect when a piece of content is missing a certain modality—like when there’s a long text that doesn’t have an audio version or when there’s an audio lecture without a transcript or video. The Media Quine would then help generate or at least prompt users to generate those missing modalities. It might suggest, “Hey, let’s create an audiobook version of this essay,” or “Let’s turn this text into a short explanatory video.” It would be a way of ensuring that the knowledge is accessible in multiple forms.</p>
<p data-start="1254" data-end="1537" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">In other words, PlenumHub wouldn’t just store information but would also help it evolve into different media, filling in the gaps so that anyone can engage with it in the format they prefer. It’s like a knowledge ecosystem that’s always trying to become more complete and accessible.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20