prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="149">Absolutely, let’s outline a list of files you’d likely need for a project like this. We’ll break them down by components so you have a clear picture.</p>
<h3 data-start="151" data-end="178">File List for PlenumHub</h3>
<h4 data-start="180" data-end="205">1. <strong data-start="188" data-end="205">Backend Files</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="206" data-end="516">
<li data-start="206" data-end="283">
<p data-start="208" data-end="283"><code data-start="208" data-end="219">server.py</code> (or <code data-start="224" data-end="233">main.rs</code> if using Rust): The main server application file.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="284" data-end="361">
<p data-start="286" data-end="361"><code data-start="286" data-end="297">models.py</code>: Definitions for your semantic data models and database schema.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="362" data-end="447">
<p data-start="364" data-end="447"><code data-start="364" data-end="381">merge_engine.py</code>: The logic for handling category-theoretic merges and versioning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="448" data-end="516">
<p data-start="450" data-end="516"><code data-start="450" data-end="468">requirements.txt</code>: List of Python dependencies (if using Python).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="518" data-end="544">2. <strong data-start="526" data-end="544">Frontend Files</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="545" data-end="729">
<li data-start="545" data-end="602">
<p data-start="547" data-end="602"><code data-start="547" data-end="559">index.html</code>: The main HTML file for the web interface.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="603" data-end="682">
<p data-start="605" data-end="682"><code data-start="605" data-end="613">app.js</code>: Your main JavaScript file, likely using React or another framework.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="683" data-end="729">
<p data-start="685" data-end="729"><code data-start="685" data-end="697">styles.css</code>: Styles for the user interface.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="731" data-end="762">3. <strong data-start="739" data-end="762">Game/Tutorial Files</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="763" data-end="1097">
<li data-start="763" data-end="1097">
<p data-start="765" data-end="800"><code data-start="765" data-end="772">game/</code> (directory for game assets)</p>
<ul data-start="803" data-end="1097">
<li data-start="803" data-end="888">
<p data-start="805" data-end="888"><code data-start="805" data-end="823">main_scene.unity</code> or <code data-start="827" data-end="844">main_scene.tscn</code>: The main 3D scene file for Unity or Godot.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="891" data-end="988">
<p data-start="893" data-end="988"><code data-start="893" data-end="912">tutorial_logic.cs</code> or <code data-start="916" data-end="935">tutorial_logic.gd</code>: Scripts that handle the interactive tutorial logic.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="991" data-end="1097">
<p data-start="993" data-end="1097"><code data-start="993" data-end="1002">assets/</code>: Folder containing 3D models, textures, and any other media needed for the game-like tutorial.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1099" data-end="1152">4. <strong data-start="1107" data-end="1152">Media Quine and Modality Conversion Files</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="1153" data-end="1327">
<li data-start="1153" data-end="1249">
<p data-start="1155" data-end="1249"><code data-start="1155" data-end="1171">media_quine.py</code>: Script that handles detecting missing modalities and triggering conversions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1250" data-end="1327">
<p data-start="1252" data-end="1327"><code data-start="1252" data-end="1268">tts_service.py</code>: Interface for text-to-speech and speech-to-text services.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1329" data-end="1372">5. <strong data-start="1337" data-end="1372">Configuration and Documentation</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="1373" data-end="1604">
<li data-start="1373" data-end="1476">
<p data-start="1375" data-end="1476"><code data-start="1375" data-end="1388">config.yaml</code>: Configuration file for setting up the platform (database connections, API keys, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1477" data-end="1561">
<p data-start="1479" data-end="1561"><code data-start="1479" data-end="1490">README.md</code>: Main documentation file explaining how to set up and run the project.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1562" data-end="1604">
<p data-start="1564" data-end="1604"><code data-start="1564" data-end="1573">LICENSE</code>: License file for the project.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1606" data-end="1620">In Summary</h3>
<p data-start="1622" data-end="1950" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">You’d have a core set of backend files for the server logic, a frontend directory for the user interface, a dedicated folder for your 3D tutorial assets and scripts, and supporting scripts for media transformation and configuration. This gives you a full picture of the file structure you’d need to get PlenumHub off the ground.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.5312