<h1 data-start="97" data-end="129">What I implemented (prototype)</h1>
<ol data-start="130" data-end="1894">
<li data-start="130" data-end="361">
<p data-start="133" data-end="156"><strong data-start="133" data-end="156">Hardened DSL parser</strong></p>
<ul data-start="160" data-end="361">
<li data-start="160" data-end="305">
<p data-start="162" data-end="305">Better parsing for <code data-start="181" data-end="211">define regexrule ... { ... }</code>, <code data-start="213" data-end="253">define typerule ... { python: &lt;expr&gt; }</code>, and <code data-start="259" data-end="304">define tokenrule ... pattern:/.../ repl:...</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="309" data-end="361">
<p data-start="311" data-end="361">Clearer error messages for malformed DSL commands.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="363" data-end="816">
<p data-start="366" data-end="405"><strong data-start="366" data-end="405">Safe TypedRule expression evaluator</strong></p>
<ul data-start="409" data-end="816">
<li data-start="409" data-end="453">
<p data-start="411" data-end="453">Uses Python <code data-start="423" data-end="428">ast</code> to validate expressions.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="457" data-end="711">
<p data-start="459" data-end="711">Allows chained <code data-start="474" data-end="504">text.method(...).method(...)</code> patterns, but <strong data-start="519" data-end="527">only</strong> when chained methods are on the <code data-start="560" data-end="566">text</code> object and only a restricted set of <code data-start="603" data-end="609">text</code> methods are permitted (<code data-start="633" data-end="642">replace</code>, <code data-start="644" data-end="651">upper</code>, <code data-start="653" data-end="660">lower</code>, <code data-start="662" data-end="669">split</code>, <code data-start="671" data-end="677">join</code>, <code data-start="679" data-end="686">strip</code>, <code data-start="688" data-end="700">capitalize</code>, <code data-start="702" data-end="709">title</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="715" data-end="816">
<p data-start="717" data-end="816">Prevents arbitrary <code data-start="736" data-end="742">eval</code> attack vectors by denying other AST nodes and by providing empty globals.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="818" data-end="1054">
<p data-start="821" data-end="852"><strong data-start="821" data-end="852">TokenRule (token-tree like)</strong></p>
<ul data-start="856" data-end="1054">
<li data-start="856" data-end="928">
<p data-start="858" data-end="928">Operates on token + whitespace pairs so replacements preserve spacing.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="932" data-end="1054">
<p data-start="934" data-end="1054">Pattern is applied to tokens (not whole text), allowing safer token-level transforms such as splitting CamelCase tokens.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1056" data-end="1151">
<p data-start="1059" data-end="1085"><strong data-start="1059" data-end="1085">RegexRule improvements</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1089" data-end="1151">
<li data-start="1089" data-end="1151">
<p data-start="1091" data-end="1151">Multiline substitution bodies supported and parsed robustly.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1153" data-end="1619">
<p data-start="1156" data-end="1182"><strong data-start="1156" data-end="1182">Minimal Flask HTTP API</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1186" data-end="1619">
<li data-start="1186" data-end="1521">
<p data-start="1188" data-end="1198">Endpoints:</p>
<ul data-start="1204" data-end="1521">
<li data-start="1204" data-end="1232">
<p data-start="1206" data-end="1232"><code data-start="1206" data-end="1217">GET /list</code> — list spheres</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1238" data-end="1272">
<p data-start="1240" data-end="1272"><code data-start="1240" data-end="1255">GET /get/&lt;id&gt;</code> — fetch a sphere</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1278" data-end="1356">
<p data-start="1280" data-end="1356"><code data-start="1280" data-end="1291">POST /add</code> — add a sphere (<code data-start="1308" data-end="1355">{"title":"...", "text":"...", "author":"..."}</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1362" data-end="1435">
<p data-start="1364" data-end="1435"><code data-start="1364" data-end="1375">POST /pop</code> — pop a sphere (<code data-start="1392" data-end="1434">{"id":"&lt;id&gt;", "rules":["rule1","rule2"]}</code>)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1441" data-end="1521">
<p data-start="1443" data-end="1521"><code data-start="1443" data-end="1456">POST /merge</code> — merge spheres (<code data-start="1474" data-end="1520">{"a":"id1","b":"id2","title":"Merged Title"}</code>)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1525" data-end="1619">
<p data-start="1527" data-end="1619">Server running on <code data-start="1545" data-end="1568">http://127.0.0.1:8765</code> in the prototype environment (development server).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1621" data-end="1894">
<p data-start="1624" data-end="1663"><strong data-start="1624" data-end="1663">Pattern/Token demo and DSL examples</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1667" data-end="1894">
<li data-start="1667" data-end="1781">
<p data-start="1669" data-end="1781">I registered <code data-start="1682" data-end="1699">normalize_punct</code> (regex), <code data-start="1709" data-end="1726">expand_acronyms</code> (typed), and a <code data-start="1742" data-end="1755">split_camel</code> (token rule) in the demo.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1785" data-end="1894">
<p data-start="1787" data-end="1894">Performed a <code data-start="1799" data-end="1804">pop</code> sequence and a <code data-start="1820" data-end="1827">merge</code>, and saved the store to <code data-start="1852" data-end="1893">/mnt/data/spherepop_enhanced_store.json</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
