<h1 data-start="2765" data-end="2801">Notes, limitations, and next steps</h1>
<ul data-start="2802" data-end="4087">
<li data-start="2802" data-end="3071">
<p data-start="2804" data-end="3071"><strong data-start="2804" data-end="2816">Security</strong>: The TypedRule evaluator is intentionally conservative: it restricts AST node types and only allows chained calls on the <code data-start="2938" data-end="2944">text</code> object with a curated method list. This is suitable for a prototype but would need more auditing for multi-tenant deployments.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3072" data-end="3244">
<p data-start="3074" data-end="3244"><strong data-start="3074" data-end="3109">Expression language alternative</strong>: If you prefer, I can replace the <code data-start="3144" data-end="3153">python:</code> expressions with a small purpose-built expression language (no AST/eval) to be even safer.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3245" data-end="3397">
<p data-start="3247" data-end="3397"><strong data-start="3247" data-end="3254">DSL</strong>: I can further harden parsing (better quoting support, escaped braces, comments) and add useful DSL features like rule namespaces and imports.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3398" data-end="3612">
<p data-start="3400" data-end="3612"><strong data-start="3400" data-end="3420">Token-tree rules</strong>: Current TokenRule operates on tokens+whitespace pairs; we can extend this to true tree-matchers (n-gram patterns, dependency-based transforms) if you provide the matching semantics you want.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3613" data-end="3784">
<p data-start="3615" data-end="3784"><strong data-start="3615" data-end="3624">Flask</strong>: The server is the Flask development server — for production we should use a WSGI server (gunicorn/uvicorn) and add authentication, rate-limiting, and logging.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3785" data-end="4087">
<p data-start="3787" data-end="3823"><strong data-start="3787" data-end="3802">Integration</strong>: Next logical steps:</p>
<ol data-start="3826" data-end="4087">
<li data-start="3826" data-end="3929">
<p data-start="3829" data-end="3929">Wire MediaQuine native TTS/STT (Whisper, MozillaTTS) and save audio artifacts to persistent storage.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3932" data-end="3994">
<p data-start="3935" data-end="3994">Add provenance (who popped/merged, timestamps, signatures).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3997" data-end="4087">
<p data-start="4000" data-end="4087">Build a tiny React front-end or game engine bridge to call the API for the 3D tutorial.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4089" data-end="4092">
<p data-start="4094" data-end="4144">If you want me to continue now, I can immediately:</p>
<ul data-start="4145" data-end="4478">
<li data-start="4145" data-end="4231">
<p data-start="4147" data-end="4231">Replace the <code data-start="4159" data-end="4168">python:</code> expression evaluation with a tiny expression language (safer).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4232" data-end="4299">
<p data-start="4234" data-end="4299">Add provenance &amp; signature metadata recording for each pop/merge.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4300" data-end="4367">
<p data-start="4302" data-end="4367">Build a minimal React demo page (static) that hits the Flask API.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4368" data-end="4478">
<p data-start="4370" data-end="4478">Integrate a mock WebSocket endpoint to push pop/merge events to a client for real-time tutorial integration.</p>
</li>
