  xleftmargin=5pt
}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\title</span></span><span>{A Formal Semantic Compute Substrate for Modular Knowledge Systems}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\author</span></span><span>{ }
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\date</span></span><span>{ }

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{document}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\maketitle</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{abstract}
Collaborative knowledge platforms currently lack a rigorous formal substrate for
typed rewriting, semantic merge guarantees, entropy bounds, and modal completeness.
We develop a categorical and rewriting-theoretic foundation for semantic knowledge
objects, specify a domain-specific transformation language with static composition
checks, present a modality-complete closure operator, and give reference grammars
and parser structure necessary to implement a mathematically sound knowledge
coordination architecture. Our approach draws on formal methods for rewrite systems
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{BaaderNipkow98}, categorical semantics of composition </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{MacLane98},
multimodal representation learning </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Baltrusaitis19}, and type-safe DSL design
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Fowler10}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{abstract}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Motivation and Requirements}

Existing collaboration infrastructures are lossy with respect to semantic invariants:
merges are textual, not meaning-preserving </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Mens02}; multimodal data is
not guaranteed to be complete </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Baltrusaitis19}; and transformation histories are not
typed as composable morphisms </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{MacLane98}.  We require a substrate that provides:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}[label=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\roman</span></span><span>*)]
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{First-class semantic objects} with typed modality fields.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Rewrite morphisms} that compose associatively and respect type constraints.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Entropy-monotone updates}, disallowing disordered merges.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Media closure}, ensuring all objects admit required modality projections.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{A transformation language} with static rule composition checking.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Semantic Object Model}

A knowledge object (semantic sphere) is a 5-tuple:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> = (I, T, M, E, S)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>I</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a unique identifier
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a human-readable title
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{V}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a modality map (e.g., text, audio, video)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is an entropy measure
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is structured metadata (authors, lineage, signatures, rule history)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

A sphere is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{modality-complete} when:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{required}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> M(k) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\neq</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emptyset</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy-Bounded Rewrite Morphisms}

A rewrite rule </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a morphism:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
r : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

which is valid if it respects an entropy budget:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

The rewrite system forms a small category </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> where composition is:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1)(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>))
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

and identity is </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>id</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Merge as a Pushout}

For spheres </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> that share a common ancestor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, merge is the colimit:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sqcup</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{colim}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

A merge is valid only if:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sqcup</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a), E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Media Closure Operator}

Define the modality completion operator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{s.t. } </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'.M </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\supseteq</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{required}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the object is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{media closed}.  Closure proceeds via learned or programmatic transducers:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{audio},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> t}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{audio}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> v}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{video}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

as in multimodal representation frameworks </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Baltrusaitis19}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Transformation Language Specification}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Grammar (EBNF)}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lstlisting}
Program      ::= Statement+
Statement    ::= PopStmt | MergeStmt | DefineRuleStmt

PopStmt      ::= "pop" ID "with" RuleChain
RuleChain    ::= Rule ( "then" Rule )*

MergeStmt    ::= "merge" ID "and" ID "as" String

DefineRuleStmt ::= RegexRule | TypeRule | TokenRule

RegexRule    ::= "define regexrule" ID "on" Modality "{" Subst+ "}"
Subst        ::= String "=&gt;" String ";"

TypeRule     ::= "define typerule" ID "input:" Modality "output:" Modality "{" PY "}"
PY           ::= "python:" Expr

TokenRule    ::= "define tokenrule" ID "on" Modality "pattern:" Regex "repl:" String

Modality     ::= "text" | "audio" | "video" | "embedding"
Regex        ::= "/" ([</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>/])+ "/"
ID           ::= [A-Za-z</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>][A-Za-z0-9</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>]*
String       ::= '"' [</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>"]* '"' | "'" [</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>']* "'"
Expr         ::= restricted expression (§5.2)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lstlisting}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Static Rule Typechecking}

Each rule declares:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
r : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{in} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{out}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

A rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is valid iff:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> i,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{out}(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{in}(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i+1})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Safe Expression Subset}

Expressions in typed rules must satisfy:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Allowed} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text.method}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{method} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{replace,upper,lower,split,join,strip,capitalize}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\big</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

No loops, imports, or arbitrary function calls are permitted, following safe embedded DSL principles </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Fowler10}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Parser Architecture}

A reference recursive descent parser follows classical designs </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Aho86,BaaderNipkow98}:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lstlisting}
parseProgram():
  while not EOF:
    statements.append(parseStatement())

parseStatement():
  if LA == "pop": return parsePop()
  if LA == "merge": return parseMerge()
  if LA == "define": return parseDefine()
  error()

parsePop():
  consume("pop"); id = consumeID()
  consume("with"); rules = parseRuleChain()
  return PopNode(id, rules)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lstlisting}

Each </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{DefineRule} node constructs a strongly typed rewrite object bound
to the rule store for subsequent composition checking.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Operational Semantics}

Pop evaluation:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i-1})
}{
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{pop}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,[r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ldots</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n]) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Merge evaluation:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{colim}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leftarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>
}{
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Discussion}

The presented substrate:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> replaces line-oriented diffs with typed semantic morphisms </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Mens02}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> enforces associative rewrite composition </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{MacLane98}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> guarantees media completeness via closure </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Baltrusaitis19}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> rejects entropy-increasing merges by construction
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> embeds transformation logic in a safe, statically analyzable DSL </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Fowler10}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

It therefore constitutes a formal compute model for knowledge, rather than a filesystem
or social graph.

