.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ---------------- Appendix: Reduction rules and algorithms ----------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>*{Appendix A: Reduction Rules and Operational Algorithms}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\addcontentsline</span></span><span>{toc}{section}{Appendix A: Reduction Rules and Operational Algorithms}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.1 Notation and preliminaries}

We recall notational conventions used in the reduction rules below.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{sphere} (semantic object) is denoted </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with components
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> = (I,T,M,E,S)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>M:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{V}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the modality map
    and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is an entropy score.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{rule} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a typed operator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{in}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{out}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
    where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>*</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes a modality (e.g. </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{text}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{audio}).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> We write </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for the result of applying rule </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
    (i.e. the rule morphism acting on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{rule chain} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes sequential application:
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)))</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> means the static type of rule </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is
    input modality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and output modality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes the entropy score of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the entropy budget of rule </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (a small nonnegative real).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes the Media-Quine completion operator producing modality closure.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.2 Small-step (micro) semantics for rule application}

We present small-step reduction rules that make rule application explicit and local.
These are useful for reasoning about provenance, incremental transforms, and concurrency.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Rule application (single step)}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.M(a)}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{where}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>' = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span> M[a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> m],</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> M[b</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a(m) ],</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') = E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
Explanation: if </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> has type </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.M(a)=m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the modality payload,
then a single reduction step </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> writes the transformed payload
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a(m)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> into modality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of the successor sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and the entropy changes by
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (annotated per rule). Implementation may represent </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as a new ID with lineage metadata that records the applied rule.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Sequential small steps (chain execution)}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{n-1}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>;r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n }
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
Sequential composition is associative by construction: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2); r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>3 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\equiv</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1; (r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>3)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
as reduction order is preserved by the chain.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.3 Big-step (macro) semantics: pop and merge}

Big-step rules summarize the effect of a multi-step evaluation into a single judgment.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Pop (big-step)}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1:a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2:a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
      </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n:a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{n-1}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n
      </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>;r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
Operational meaning: the judgment </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> asserts that applying the rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R=r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>;r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> produces </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, where all intermediate steps are type-correct and the chain preserves per-step entropy budgets.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Merge validity and pushout semantics}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be spheres where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> represents shared ancestry
or explicitly provided structural overlap. The abstract merge (categorical pushout)
is denoted </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{pushout}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and is computed subject to entropy constraints:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{pushout}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
      E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a),E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{merge}}}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If the entropy inequality does not hold the merge is either rejected or requires mediation
(i.e. insertion of additional rewrite morphisms </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that transitive merge yields acceptable entropy).

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.4 Media-Quine (closure) rules}

Media-Quine </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> attempts to fill missing modalities. We give small-step synthesis rules
that are either programmatic transducers or learned models.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Detection of missing modality}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{required}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.M(k) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varnothing</span></span><span>}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{missing}(k)} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
This is a zero-change detection step used to trigger synthesis.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Synthesis (text </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> audio) step}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.M(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{text}) = t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ available}}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{where}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'.M(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{audio}) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a}(t)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
Analogous rules exist for </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> t}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (STT), </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> v}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (text-to-video), and embedding extractors.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Closure judgment}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{*}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{synthesis}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{K}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{required}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'.M(k)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\neq</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varnothing</span></span><span>}
     {Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is idempotent: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q(Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)) = Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.5 Typed rule checking and chain validation}

To ensure statically-checked correctness of rule chains we use the following judgments.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Rule typing}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{rule }r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ declared with input } a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ and output } b}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r : a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Chain well-formedness}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 : a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 : a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n : a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{n-1}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n}
     {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{chain}} r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>; r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n : a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If any adjacent pair fails to align, the chain is rejected at parse/analysis time.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.6 Confluence and determinism concerns}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Local confluence of non-overlapping rules}

If two rules </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> operate on disjoint modalities (i.e. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r:a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>s:c</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> d</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ne</span></span><span> c</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>)
then they commute:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
r(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>s(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>) = s(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>r(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Such commuting rules produce locally confluent reductions.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Critical pairs and conflict resolution}

When rules overlap (e.g. both read and write a shared modality) critical pairs must be resolved.
We recommend policy-driven resolution:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Entropy-preference}: choose the branch that minimizes the resulting entropy.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Authoritative provenance}: prefer the rewrite that preserves higher provenance weight.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Manual mediation}: produce a merged candidate and emit a human-review task.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Formally, if </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r,s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> produce distinct successors </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>s</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> then compute
a mediated merge candidate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{mediate}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>s)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and accept only if
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\min</span></span><span>(E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r),E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>s))+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{mediate}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.7 Reference algorithm: reduction engine}

The following pseudocode is a compact specification of a reduction engine that
implements parsing, typing, rule application (pop), merge, and Media-Quine completion.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lstlisting}[language=,basicstyle=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ttfamily</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\small</span></span><span>]
</span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> input: statement (pop/merge/define), global rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store, sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store
function execute</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>statement(stmt):
  match stmt:
    case DefineRule(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>decl):
      rule = compile</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>rule(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>decl)
      rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.add(rule.name, rule)
      return OK

    case Pop(id, rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>chain):
      sigma = sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.get(id)
      </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> static typecheck the chain
      if not typecheck</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>chain(rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>chain, rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store): error("type mismatch")
      current = sigma
      for r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>name in rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>chain:
        r = rule</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.get(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>name)
        </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> check entropy budget locally
        if E(current) + r.delta &gt; current.entropy</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>budget + r.epsilon:
          error("entropy budget exceeded: require mediation")
        current = apply</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>rule(r, current)   </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> produces new sphere object with lineage metadata
      </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> persist popped sphere
      sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.put(current.id, current)
      return current

    case Merge(a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>id, b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>id, title):
      a = sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.get(a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>id); b = sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.get(b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>id)
      ancestor = find</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>ancestor(a,b)  </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> may be None
      candidate = compute</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>pushout(a, ancestor, b)
      if E(candidate) &lt;= max(E(a), E(b)) + MERGE</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>EPS:
        sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.put(candidate.id, candidate)
        return candidate
      else:
        </span><span><span class="hljs-params">#</span></span><span> attempt mediation by applying candidate rewrite rules or alert human
        mediated = attempt</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>mediation(a,b,candidate)
        if E(mediated) &lt;= max(E(a),E(b)) + MERGE</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>EPS:
          sphere</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>store.put(mediated.id, mediated); return mediated
        error("merge failed: entropy constraint")
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lstlisting}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span>
Auxiliary functions:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{typecheck</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>chain(chain, store)}: verify </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{chain}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> by looking up rule types.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{apply</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>rule(r, sigma)}: run </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to produce </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and record lineage.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{compute</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>pushout(a, anc, b)}: compute structural colimit (implementation-specific).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{attempt</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>mediation(a,b,candidate)}: generate mediated candidates (e.g., via local rewrites) and select best by entropy.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.8 Complexity and implementation remarks}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Type checking} is linear in the number of rules in a chain (lookup per rule): </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O(n)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Rule application} cost depends on modality size (e.g. text length) and model complexity (TTS/STT costs dominate for media synthesis).
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Merging} (pushout) complexity depends on the chosen structural representation; naive textual merging is linear in content size, but semantic structural merges (schema alignment) can be NP-hard in the worst case; heuristics and incremental mediation are recommended.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Concurrency control}: implement optimistic concurrency with entropy-based merge validation at commit time.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.9 Correctness properties and guarantees}

We summarize guarantees the system aims to provide subject to correct implementations and trusted rule-store:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Type safety}: well-typed rule chains will not perform modality mismatches at runtime.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Entropy discipline}: all accepted pops and merges respect declared entropy budgets; merges that would increase entropy beyond thresholds are rejected or mediated.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Provenance completeness}: every produced sphere contains lineage metadata recording the sequence of rule morphisms applied.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Idempotent closure}: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is idempotent and ensures media completeness when successful.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Local confluence for disjoint rules}: reductions commuting on disjoint modalities are confluent.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>*{A.10 Examples (worked reductions)}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Example 1: pop with acronym expansion and summary}

Given sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.M(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{text}) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{``RSVP models...''}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and rule chain
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{expand</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>acro};</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{summarize}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> where
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{expand</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>acro}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{type}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{summarize}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{text}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{expand</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>acro}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{summarize}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
and the engine persists </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> annotated with provenance </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{popped</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\_</span></span><span>from}=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>.I</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Example 2: merge rejection by entropy budget}

If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a)=5</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)=6</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and the computed pushout </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m)=12</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> while
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}}=0.5</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the inequality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>12 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(5,6)+0.5</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> fails and the merge is rejected or deferred for mediation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span> This appendix provides a concise operational specification and reduction theory suitable for rigorous implementation and verification.  It is intentionally algorithmic and type-oriented so that language implementers and system architects can map each judgment to concrete checks in an interpreter or runtime.
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ---------------- end appendix ----------------</span></span><span>
