.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{PlenumHub: Execution Model and Semantic Consensus}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:plenumhub}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

PlenumHub is the distributed execution substrate that runs SpherePOP programs at scale, maintaining global semantic consistency while allowing decentralized contribution and asynchronous evolution. Where version control systems synchronize files and social networks synchronize feeds, PlenumHub synchronizes </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{semantic state transitions}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Global state as a semantic field}

Rather than a repository or timeline, the system state is a live field:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2, ..., </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Partitions of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> may reside on different peers, but consensus is formed not on literal content, but on </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{validity of transformations}:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Consensus}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Leftrightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ and } </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nexists</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ entropy violations}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Smart propagation: rule diffusion instead of content sync}

Nodes do not transitively gossip raw data. Instead, they propagate:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> rule declarations </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> sphere identifiers and proofs of validity
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> rule execution certificates </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> entropy compliance proofs </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)+</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

This decouples semantic validity from local storage and avoids exponential content replication.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Conflict resolution as entropy mediation}

When peers propose conflicting sphere updates:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\not</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sim</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

the network does not adopt a winner, but attempts mediation:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{mediate}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{such that} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a),E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If no such </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> exists, the conflict is marked as an unresolved semantic divergence rather than overwritten.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Curricular update scheduling}

To approximate Kumar’s staged learning principle </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{akarsh2023platonic,bengio2009curriculum}, PlenumHub prioritizes rule-chains that:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> grow modality completeness,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> reduce entropy variance between neighboring spheres,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> increase factor independence,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> introduce minimal structural disruption.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

Which formalizes a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{curriculum on semantic topology}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Liveness guarantees}

PlenumHub ensures:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{align*}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Safety:} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Never commit an entropy-violating sphere} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Liveness:} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{All valid rule cascades eventually propagate} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Convergence:} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Closed spheres approach fixed points under } Q </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{align*}

