</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tabular}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{table}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Resulting paradigm}

PlenumHub is:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> not a database but a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{semantic phase space},
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> not a feed but a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{transformation manifold},
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> not a social network but a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{meaning propagation medium},
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> not version control but </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{lawful evolution of ideas}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

With these mechanics defined, we now turn to implementation-level operational semantics (Appendix A) and interpreter design.
