01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Interpreter and Runtime Algorithms}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:interpreter}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

This section specifies an executable semantics for the Semantic Plenum platform: the SpherePOP evaluator, rule-engine interpreter, and PlenumHub runtime. These algorithms are presented abstractly and deterministically, with nondeterministic mediation points made explicit. The design goal is not maximal performance but </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{semantic determinism, entropy safety}, and </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{typed transformation correctness}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Core runtime state}

A node in the PlenumHub network maintains the following local state:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{N} = (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{Q}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the local sphere store,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the rule library (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with entropy budgets),
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{Q}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the event queue of pending SpherePOP operations,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a proof cache of previously validated reductions.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

The system evolves by consuming events from </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{Q}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, validating them, executing them if admissible, and emitting proofs.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Event grammar}

The interpreter processes four event forms:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
e </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\left</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{array}{l}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{MakeSphere}(I, T, M) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Pop}(A, B, R) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge}(A, B) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Close}(A)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{array}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\right</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Each event reduces to a sphere transition </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> or fails.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Main interpreter loop}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{verbatim}<span class="hljs-string">
while Q not empty:
    e = dequeue(Q)
    if not WellTyped(e): continue
    if not EntropyAdmissible(e): continue
    result = Reduce(e)
    if result.success:
        Phi.add(result.sphere)
        P.cache(result.proof)
        Broadcast(result.proof)
    else:
        Mediate(e)
</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{verbatim}

This loop ensures </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{only valid reductions enter the semantic field}.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Well-typedness rules}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{WellTyped}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{MakeSphere}) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\forall</span></span><span> k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> T, M(k) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ is well-formed}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{WellTyped}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Pop}(A,B,R)) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> R : T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{WellTyped}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge}(A,B)) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{compatible}(T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A,T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{WellTyped}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Close}(A)) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{sphere } A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ exists}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy admissibility}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{EntropyAdmissible}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Pop}(A,B,R)) := E(R(A)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(B) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{EntropyAdmissible}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Merge}(A,B)) := E(A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span> B) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(A),E(B)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{EntropyAdmissible}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Close}(A)) := E(Q(A)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(A) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>Q
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If entropy bounds fail, the event is not discarded but routed to mediation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Reduction semantics}

Valid reductions produce a new sphere and proof certificate:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Reduce}(e) =
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{cases}
(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>', </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{if admissible} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{otherwise}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{cases}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a machine-verifiable object containing:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> e,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{before}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{after}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{before}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{after}},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{rule-justification} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Proofs allow remote nodes to replay or audit semantic transitions without replaying content.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Media-Quine closure operator}

Closure is computed lazily but validated eagerly:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{verbatim}<span class="hljs-string">
function Close(A):
    sigma = Phi.get(A)
    while missing modality k in sigma:
        sigma.M[k] = Synthesize(k, sigma)
    if entropy(sigma) &lt;= E(A) + eps_Q:
        return sigma
    else:
        return FAIL
</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{verbatim}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\noindent</span></span><span> Closure is idempotent: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Close(Close(A))} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\texttt</span></span><span>{Close(A)}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Mediation protocol}

When reduction fails:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{verbatim}<span class="hljs-string">
function Mediate(e):
    candidates = RewriteSearch(e)
    for c in candidates:
        if EntropyAdmissible(c) and WellTyped(c):
            enqueue(Q, c)
            return
    LogConflict(e)
</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{verbatim}

Mediation searches for equivalent programs, alternate rewrite paths, or entropy-lowering preconditions. Exhaustive search is avoided by bounding rewrite depth.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Network propagation}

Nodes do not broadcast spheres, only proofs:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Broadcast}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{peers apply }</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ if valid}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

A peer accepts a proof if:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Verify}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) := </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{signature valid} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\wedge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{entropy bounds respected} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\wedge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{typing derivation correct}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This makes consensus a function of proof validity, not data replication.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Determinism and convergence properties}

The system guarantees:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{align*}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Semantic safety} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{No ill-typed sphere enters } </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Entropy safety} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: E </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{ never increases without certified budget} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Convergence of closure} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: Q(Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)) = Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Proof convergence} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{All peers accepting a proof reach identical state} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{align*}

However, the system is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{not} confluent in general because mediation introduces branching semantic histories:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{and} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\not</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Instead, it satisfies </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{bounded divergence}:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1), E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

ensuring no branch drifts into semantic incoherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Interpreter complexity}

Let:

- </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = spheres in local store,
- </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = average rule-chain length,
- </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = modalities per sphere.

Then:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Type checking: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>O(r)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Entropy checking: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>O(1)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Merkle-style proof verification: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>O(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span> n)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Closure synthesis: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>O(m </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{synth}})</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

where </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\(</span></span><span>C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{synth}}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\)</span></span><span> is the cost of the least expensive missing modality synthesis path.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Summary}

The runtime realizes the design principles:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> knowledge evolves through certified transformations, not overwrites,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> entropy bounds stabilize meaning against synthetic drift,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> closure guarantees modality completeness,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> proofs replace content gossip,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> mediation replaces consensus-by-loss,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> and interpretation is semantic, not syntactic.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

This completes the executable specification of the Semantic Plenum interpreter.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
