.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Security, Adversarial Stability, and Semantic Attacks}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:security}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

A semantic network is not merely a communication substrate but an evolving model of shared reality. Attacks therefore target not only availability or confidentiality, but the integrity of meaning itself. We define the threat model, characterize semantic attack surfaces, and formalize guarantees that limit adversarial influence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Threat model}

Adversaries may attempt to:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> inject high-entropy spheres to destabilize shared meaning,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> bypass symmetry invariants via malformed rule chains,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> trigger Media--Quine completion into hallucinated modalities,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> engineer merges that exceed entropy budgets,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> or construct rule cycles that simulate validity without semantics.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Crucially, unlike content platforms, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{misinformation is not the primary attack vector}—structural destabilization is.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic attack classes}

We categorize attacks as follows:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tabular}{ll}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\toprule</span></span><span>
Attack </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Intent </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\midrule</span></span><span>
Entropy flooding </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Increase </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Phi</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> without bound </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Type forgery </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Spoof rule signatures to evade validation </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Closure hallucination </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Exploit </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to infer unsupported modalities </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Merge poisoning </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Force semantically incoherent </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span> B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Equivariance breaking </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Apply non-symmetric transforms undetected </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Rule looping </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Create valid but semantically empty cycles </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bottomrule</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tabular}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Bounds on structural corruption}

We define </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{semantic drift} of a sphere trajectory </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
D = E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n) - E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

The runtime enforces:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
D </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{n} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Thus an attacker cannot induce unbounded disorder without controlling an unbounded number of valid entropy budgets, each cryptographically signed and rate-limited.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Proof-level verification}

Since nodes exchange proofs </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> instead of state, a forged transformation must satisfy:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Verify}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span>) = 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid signature} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\land</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{type correctness} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\land</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{entropy admissible}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Failure to satisfy any clause causes silent rejection without network amplification.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Closure safety via synthesis whitelisting}

To prevent hallucinated modality injection, closure operators </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> used in Media--Quine completion must be drawn from an auditable, deterministic, versioned model registry:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{T}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{approved}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\wedge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{hash}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\tau</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{consensus}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This prevents adversarial model substitution.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Merge detoxification}

When a merge produces unacceptable entropy yet remains type-valid, nodes attempt bounded mediation:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\exists</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A, R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{s.t.} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
E(R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>A(A) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>B(B)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(A), E(B)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

If no such rewrite exists within bounded search depth, the merge is permanently quarantined rather than approximated.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Guarantees}

The system provides the following security properties:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Entropy safety}: disorder cannot grow faster than signed entropy budgets permit.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Type integrity}: no sphere can be malformed without invalidating all downstream proofs.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Equivariance preservation}: illegal symmetry-breaking rewrites cannot validate.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Closure authenticity}: synthesized modalities are traceable to certified generators.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Quarantine stability}: failed merges cannot contaminate the global field.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Resulting threat containment}

Unlike content-moderation defenses, which attempt to classify meaning </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{after} publication, this system constrains the production of unstable meaning </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{before} consensus. Security is thus achieved not by filtering content, but by restricting valid state transitions.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
