</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Proof Theory: Soundness, Progress, and Entropy Invariants}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:proof-theory}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

In this section we establish formal guarantees for the Semantic Plenum calculus. We prove three critical properties:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Type soundness}: valid reductions never produce ill-typed spheres or invalid modality accesses.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Progress}: well-formed SpherePOP programs either take a reduction step or are values (closed spheres).
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Entropy boundedness}: semantic entropy never increases except under certified, budgeted rules.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

These properties ensure that knowledge evolution cannot diverge into meaningless structure, malformed modality states, or unbounded semantic disorder.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Preliminaries}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

We recall key judgments:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>: sphere satisfies its type signature and modality requirements.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> R : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>: rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is well-typed.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>: sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> reduces to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> under rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>: entropy of sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

We also use the admissibility predicate:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{Admissible}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{R} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\iff</span></span><span> 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> R : T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\wedge</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Type Soundness}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 1 (Type Preservation).}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof.}  
Reduction only occurs if:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> R : T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (type-checking passed), and
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> each rule </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> reads and writes only declared modalities.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

No rule may introduce a new modality not in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, remove a required modality, or write to an untyped channel. Therefore </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfies its signature and remains valid. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Corollary 1.1 (No Invalid Modality Access).}
A well-typed SpherePOP program never references a missing or untyped modality during execution.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Progress}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 2 (Progress).}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> then either:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is in Media-Quine closure (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, no reductions apply), or
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> there exists a rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof sketch.}  
Because:

1. Every required modality type is declared in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
2. The closure operator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> can generate any missing modality using approved transducers,
3. At least identity and closure rules are always available,

then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> cannot be stuck in an unproductive non-closed state. Either closure applies or a typed rule chain applies. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Corollary 2.1 (Deadlock Freedom for Valid Spheres).}
There is no reachable </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> such that </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> but no reduction or closure rule applies.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy Boundedness}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 3 (Local Entropy Bound).}
For any single reduction </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xrightarrow</span></span><span>{r} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof.}  
This is enforced by rule admissibility in the interpreter. Execution halts or diverts to mediation when the bound is violated. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 4 (Global Entropy Bound for Rule Chains).}
For a composed rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R = r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1;</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>;r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>R </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{i=1}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>k </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof.}  
Follows by repeated application of Theorem 3 and induction on chain length. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Corollary 4.1 (No Unbounded Semantic Drift).}
Entropy cannot increase without a corresponding sum of signed entropy budgets. Therefore:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0) + B
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>B</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the total entropy budget of all accepted rule certificates in the causal history.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy Safety Under Merge}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 5 (Merge Entropy Guarantee).}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is accepted, then:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a), E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b)) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof.}  
Merge events are admitted if and only if this inequality holds. All other merges are rejected or mediated. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Corollary 5.1 (Semantic Heat Death is Unreachable).}
A sequence of valid merges cannot monotonically diverge to infinite entropy, since each merge admits at most a bounded and signed increase.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Confluence, Divergence, and Determinism}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

Unlike lambda calculi, this system is not globally confluent, since multiple valid knowledge trajectories may exist. However it satisfies the weaker property:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 6 (Bounded Divergence).}
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
|E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1) - E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2)| </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1} + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Thus semantic trajectories may diverge in content, but not without bound in disorder.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic Consensus Safety}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Theorem 7 (Consensus Validity).}
If all peers verify proofs before accepting state transition, then all accepted spheres satisfy:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{valid} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\wedge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 + B
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

independent of network ordering.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Proof.}  
Peers never accept unverified proofs, and proofs enforce typing and entropy contracts. </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\square</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Summary of Guarantees}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ------------------------------------------------------------</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tabular}{ll}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\toprule</span></span><span>
Property </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Guarantee </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\midrule</span></span><span>
Type Safety </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> No ill-typed sphere is reachable </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Progress </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Valid spheres are never stuck </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Entropy Safety </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Disorder is budgeted, never unbounded </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Merge Safety </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Fusion preserves entropy limits </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Closure Stability </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q(Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)) = Q(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Consensus Soundness </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> Peers never accept invalid transitions </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Divergence Control </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> All divergence is entropy-bounded </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\bottomrule</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tabular}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

These results establish that PlenumHub forms a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{thermodynamically disciplined proof-carrying semantic runtime}, in which knowledge can evolve but cannot destabilize, collapse, or become ill-typed without explicit, auditable rule expenditure. This completes the formal core of the system.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
