f instructions</strong> for expanding and extending the essay while preserving its structure and intent:</p>
<hr data-start="138" data-end="141">
<h3 data-start="143" data-end="195"><strong data-start="147" data-end="195">1. Strengthen the motivation and positioning</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="196" data-end="656">
<li data-start="196" data-end="361">
<p data-start="198" data-end="361">Expand the opening to clearly situate PlenumHub as a successor to GitHub and social platforms with semantic integrity, causal attribution, and modality completion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="362" data-end="537">
<p data-start="364" data-end="537">Explicitly connect this to failures of current systems (content collapse, missing provenance, fragmented media, lossy translation between modalities, and opaque governance).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="538" data-end="656">
<p data-start="540" data-end="656">Add a comparison table: <em data-start="564" data-end="607">GitHub vs. Social Platforms vs. PlenumHub</em> (features, failure modes, epistemic guarantees).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="658" data-end="661">
<h3 data-start="663" data-end="708"><strong data-start="667" data-end="708">2. Deepen the mathematical foundation</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="709" data-end="1237">
<li data-start="709" data-end="938">
<p data-start="711" data-end="747">Provide full formal definitions for:</p>
<ul data-start="750" data-end="938">
<li data-start="750" data-end="791">
<p data-start="752" data-end="791">SpherePop state space <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.075em;">S</span></span></span></span></p>
