rt="0" data-end="112">Understood. Here is a <strong data-start="22" data-end="70">clean, revised set of expansion instructions</strong> with your corrections and tone preserved:</p>
<hr data-start="114" data-end="117">
<h2 data-start="119" data-end="176"><strong data-start="122" data-end="176">Instructions for Expanding and Extending the Essay</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="178" data-end="255"><strong data-start="182" data-end="255">1. Rewrite the opening section to justify the necessity of the system</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="256" data-end="840">
<li data-start="256" data-end="396">
<p data-start="258" data-end="396">Frame the core problem as <strong data-start="284" data-end="396">semantic fragmentation, provenance loss, modality incompleteness, and ungrounded synchronization of meaning.</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="397" data-end="480">
<p data-start="399" data-end="480">Present PlenumHub as a <strong data-start="422" data-end="456">coherence-first infrastructure</strong> rather than a platform.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="481" data-end="774">
<p data-start="483" data-end="571">Show conceptually how SpherePop calculus, modality completion, and quorate merges solve:</p>
<ul data-start="574" data-end="774">
<li data-start="574" data-end="589">
<p data-start="576" data-end="589">meaning drift</p>
</li>
<li data-start="592" data-end="617">
<p data-start="594" data-end="617">unverifiable authorship</p>
</li>
<li data-start="620" data-end="646">
<p data-start="622" data-end="646">missing media modalities</p>
</li>
<li data-start="649" data-end="692">
<p data-start="651" data-end="692">lossy translation between representations</p>
</li>
<li data-start="695" data-end="725">
<p data-start="697" data-end="725">non-composable collaboration</p>
</li>
<li data-start="728" data-end="774">
<p data-start="730" data-end="774">governance by attention instead of structure</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="775" data-end="840">
<p data-start="777" data-end="840">Remove any early GitHub comparison; defer it to later sections.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="842" data-end="845">
<h3 data-start="847" data-end="886"><strong data-start="851" data-end="886">2. Deepen the mathematical core</strong></h3>
<p data-start="887" data-end="921">Introduce and prove properties of:</p>
