<p data-start="4588" data-end="4617">Notes and minimal suggestions</p>
<ul data-start="4618" data-end="5011">
<li data-start="4618" data-end="4776">
<p data-start="4620" data-end="4776">If you want a version in a separate PDF as an asset, I can output a standalone <code data-start="4699" data-end="4712">tikzpicture</code> wrapped with <code data-start="4726" data-end="4738">standalone</code> class (good for export to SVG/PNG).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4777" data-end="4882">
<p data-start="4779" data-end="4882">I can also (optionally) add colored fills, icons, or animate the proof flow for a presentation slide.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4883" data-end="5011">
<p data-start="4885" data-end="5011">If you want the diagram to match your document fonts exactly, compile with <code data-start="4960" data-end="4969">xelatex</code>/<code data-start="4970" data-end="4980">lualatex</code> and your chosen font packages.</p>
</li>
</ul>
