</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{A1. String Diagram Calculus for Sphere Morphisms}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:string-diagrams}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

While the algebra of Section~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{sec:cat-foundations} guarantees that SpherePOP forms a symmetric monoidal category, it remains difficult to reason about composite rule flows purely symbolically. We therefore provide a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{string diagram} presentation, which exposes the causal topology of semantic transformations, merges, forks, and closure completion.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Basic Diagram Conventions}

We adopt the following graphical syntax:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}[itemsep=3pt]
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Wires} represent semantic spheres </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Boxes} represent rule morphisms </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Juxtaposition} (horizontal placement) denotes monoidal product </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Vertical composition} denotes rule chain composition </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Braiding} represents symmetry isomorphism </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Caps and cups} are duality morphisms used to express mediation and feedback.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vspace</span></span><span>{6pt}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  every node/.style={font=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\small</span></span><span>},
  morph/.style={draw, rounded corners, inner sep=4pt, fill=gray!10},
  &gt;=Stealth
]

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% identity wire</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (0,0) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,-0.2) -- (0,-1);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (0,-1.2) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% morphism box</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (2.5,-0.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (2.5,0) -- (2.5,-0.3);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (2.5,-0.9) -- (2.5,-1.2);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (2.5,-1.4) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% tensor product</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (4,-0.2) -- (4,-1);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (4,-1.2) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (4.8,-0.2) -- (4.8,-1);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (4.8,-1.2) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (4.4,0.1) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}

These components compose to express multi-sphere rule flows.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Sequential Rule Composition}

A rule chain </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>''</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is written:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  morph/.style={draw, rounded corners, fill=gray!10},
  &gt;=Stealth
]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0,0) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0,-1.2) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.3) -- (0,-0.3);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,-0.9) -- (0,-1.5);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This enforces that intermediate sphere typing and entropy budgets must align at the internal wire.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Parallel Evolution via Tensor}

Two spheres evolving independently under rules </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  morph/.style={draw, rounded corners, fill=gray!10},
  &gt;=Stealth
]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0,0) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (1.5,0) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.3) -- (0,-0.3);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (1.5,0.3) -- (1.5,-0.3);

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (0,-0.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (1.5,-0.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This expresses </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Symmetry (Wire Crossing)}

Sphere order may be exchanged by the symmetry isomorphism:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[&gt;=Stealth]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.2) -- (1,-0.6);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (1,0.2) -- (0,-0.6);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (-0.2,0.3) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (1.2,0.3) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (-0.2,-0.8) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (1.2,-0.8) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

 This depicts the isomorphism </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b}: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Entropy-Gated Merge}

Merging is a partial commutative monoid operation that consumes two spheres and emits one only if entropy constraints are respected:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  morph/.style={draw, rounded corners, fill=gray!10},
  &gt;=Stealth
]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.3) -- (0,-0.2);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (1,0.3) -- (1,-0.2);

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0.5,-0.5) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0.5,-0.8) -- (0.5,-1.2);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (0.5,-1.4) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

The operation is undefined (diagram fails to typecheck) if </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m) &gt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\max</span></span><span>(E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a, E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{merge}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Media–Quine Closure}

The closure operator is drawn as a self-looping projector:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  morph/.style={draw, circle, inner sep=2pt, fill=gray!10},
  &gt;=Stealth
]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.3) -- (0,-0.2);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0,-0.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,-1) .. controls (0.8,-1.4) and (0.8,0) .. (0,-0.4);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Idempotence requires that the loop adds no new modalities when reapplied.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Full Interaction: Pop → Merge → Close}

A complete multi-sphere evolution pipeline appears as:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[
  morph/.style={draw, rounded corners, fill=gray!10, inner sep=4pt},
  &gt;=Stealth
]
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% input wires</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,0.6) -- (0,0.1);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (0,0.8) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (2,0.6) -- (2,0.1);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (2,0.8) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% pop boxes</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (0,-0.3) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (2,-0.3) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% wires into merge</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (0,-0.8) -- (0,-1.2);
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (2,-0.8) -- (2,-1.2);

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (1,-1.5) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\oplus</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (1,-1.8) -- (1,-2.2);

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% closure</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[morph] at (1,-2.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Q</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;, thick] (1,-2.9) -- (1,-3.3);

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (1,-3.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{closed}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This expresses:
1. two independent pops,  
2. entropy-guarded merge,  
3. stabilization under modality completion.

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Interpretive Summary}

String diagrams make explicit properties that are otherwise obscured in formula notation:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Causality}: which sphere influences which intermediate state.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Concurrency}: independent rewrites occur without interference.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Symmetry}: wire crossings are structural, not computational.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Invalid merges}: untypable diagrams correspond to invalid semantic operations.
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Normalization}: closure is a projector, not an arbitrary generator.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Diagrammatic reasoning exposes that PlenumHub is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{not a rewriting system with metadata} but a genuine </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{string-diagrammatic calculus of meaning transport with entropy bounds and modality completion constraints}.

</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
