</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{A2. Free Symmetric Monoidal Category Generated by Semantic Rules}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:free-smc}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

While the previous section showed that semantic sphere evolution </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{behaves like} a symmetric monoidal category (SMC), we now make this construction precise by exhibiting </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{free SMC generated by typed rule morphisms} modulo entropy-compatibility and modality typing constraints.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Generators}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the set of modality types (text, audio, code, proof, embedding, etc.).  
Define a generating signature </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(G,O)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> where:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the set of base objects (one object per modality),
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>G = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span> r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mid</span></span><span> a,b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> O,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a set of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{rule generators} equipped with entropy budgets.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

We interpret each generator </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as an atomic SpherePOP transformation acting on modality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and producing modality </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with entropy cost bounded by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Free Symmetric Monoidal Construction}

The </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{free symmetric monoidal category} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> generated by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(G,O)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> consists of:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Objects}: all finite multimodal tensors of base objects:
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
      X = m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdots</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M},
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
    interpreted as required modality signatures </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>T = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dots</span></span><span>,m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>k</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
    
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Morphisms}: formal string diagrams built from:
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> generators </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> identities </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> tensor product </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> composition </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
            </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> symmetry wires </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{x,y} : x</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> y</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> x</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
        </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}
        modulo the standard SMC coherence relations (associativity, unit, symmetry, hexagon).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Quotienting by Semantic Validity}

Not all morphisms of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are valid semantic evolutions.  
We impose two semantic congruences:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}[label=(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alph</span></span><span>*)]
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Entropy admissibility}: A morphism </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is invalid if accumulated entropy along any computational path exceeds the sphere budget:
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> R} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(r) &gt; E</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{max}}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Modality typing}: A morphism is invalid if it attempts to apply </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>r:a</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> to an object tensor not containing </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>a</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

Define the quotient category:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G) / {</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{entropy, type}}}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sim</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{entropy, type}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> identifies only those diagrams that:

1. are equal under standard SMC axioms, **and**
2. respect entropy budget and modality preconditions.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Universal Property}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Universal Mapping Property]
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be any symmetric monoidal category equipped with:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> a modality assignment functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>O : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Obj}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> entropy-bounded arrows </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>G(r</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i):F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>O(a)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>O(b)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for each generator,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}
such that entropy is subadditive under composition.

Then there exists a unique strict monoidal functor:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{F} : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
preserving symmetry and entropy bounds.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
By freeness of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, any generator assignment extends uniquely to a strict SMC functor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{F}:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.  
Because </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> respects entropy monotonicity and typing, morphisms violating entropy or modality conditions collapse to invalid maps in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, so </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\hat</span></span><span>{F}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> factors uniquely through the quotient </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{F}(G)/{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sim</span></span><span>}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, yielding the required functor.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Interpretation}

This result establishes that:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> SpherePOP is </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{not an ad-hoc rewrite system} but the </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{free SMC on meaning-preserving rule generators under entropy constraints}.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Any other semantic system that respects entropy, symmetry, and modality typing factors uniquely through PlenumHub.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Rule libraries extend PlenumHub the same way algebraic theories extend equational logic: by </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{adding generators, not altering structure}.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No alternative substrate can express strictly more lawful compositions without either:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\newline</span></span><span>
        (i) violating entropy typing, or</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\newline</span></span><span>
        (ii) embedding SpherePOP as a subtheory.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Corollaries}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[No Hidden Rewrites]
All valid semantic rewrites are representable as string diagrams in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. There are no valid transformations outside the generated space.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[Rule Library Completeness]
Adding new permitted rule generators extends the category conservatively; it never invalidates prior derivations.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{corollary}[Semantic Interoperability]
Any knowledge system whose transformations are typed, entropy-bounded, and compositional admits a semantics-preserving embedding into PlenumHub.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{corollary}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Conclusion}

By constructing PlenumHub as a free symmetric monoidal category with entropy-typed generators, we recover a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{universal algebra of semantic composition}. This elevates knowledge evolution from:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{“a history of edits”}  
to  
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{“a lawful diagram of meaning flow.”}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
