01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{A3. Coherence Theorems for PlenumHub}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:coherence}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

Having established </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> as the free symmetric monoidal category (SMC) on entropy-typed rule generators, we now prove coherence: that all valid SpherePOP diagram rewrites reduce uniquely up to SMC isomorphism, and that entropy annotations do not break coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Monoidal Structure}

The monoidal product </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> on semantic objects (modality tensors) satisfies:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Associator:}  
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y,Z} : (X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Left/Right unitors:}  
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>X : I </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,  
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>X : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> I </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Symmetry (braiding):}  
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y} : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,  
    </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{Y,X} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Each carries zero entropy cost:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\lambda</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span>) = 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
since they express information re-wiring, not semantic transformation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Pentagon Coherence}

For any four semantic objects </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>W,X,Y,Z</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the associator diagrams commute:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xymatrix</span></span><span>{
((W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{W,X,Y} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{W</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X,Y,Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
(W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{W,X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y,Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> ((X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y,Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
(W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{W,X,Y</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
W </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z))
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Entropy Preservation]
All paths through the pentagon accumulate zero entropy, so coherence respects entropy budgets.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
Each associator contributes </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>=0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and composition is additive in entropy. Hence all paths have total entropy </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, so the pentagon remains entropy-neutral.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Hexagon Coherence}

Symmetry interacts coherently with associativity according to the hexagon axioms:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\xymatrix</span></span><span>{
(X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y,Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y, Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X, Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
(Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Z) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{Y,Z,X}} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\alpha</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{Z,X,Y}} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>
(Z </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> X) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> Y
}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

and symmetrically for the inverse hexagon.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Braiding Is Entropy-Neutral]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\gamma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{X,Y}) = 0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, so permutation of modalities does not consume entropy budget.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Interchange Law for Rule Composition}

For rule morphisms </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f, g, h, k</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
(f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> (h </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> k) = (f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> h) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> (g </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> k)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This guarantees parallel semantic edits compose independently when applied to disjoint modality channels.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Additivity of Entropy under Interchange]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>((f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> (h </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> k)) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(g) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(h) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(k)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
Tensor and composition each preserve additivity of entropy:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(g), </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> h) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(h)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Substituting into both sides yields equality.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Global Coherence}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Coherence of Entropy-Typed SpherePOP Diagrams]
Any two well-typed SpherePOP string diagrams with the same source and target are equal if and only if they are related by a sequence of:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> identity, associator, unitor, and braiding rewrites,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> entropy-preserving interchange,
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> generator equality modulo entropy budget.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}

Thus diagram equality is decidable up to SMC isomorphism.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{proof}
By Mac Lane coherence for symmetric monoidal categories, SMC diagrams commute up to structural isomorphism. Because entropy annotations are additive, non-negative, and zero on all structural morphisms, entropy forms a monoidal functor:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span> : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> (</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0}, +, 0)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
which preserves diagram equality, so coherence lifts without obstruction.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{proof}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Implications for PlenumHub}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Every allowed semantic history collapses to a unique string diagram up to canonical isomorphism.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No hidden order-dependence exists outside entropy expenditure.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Consensus merges correspond to canonical diagram composites, not voting or linear precedence.
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Mode-crossing permutations are free (entropy </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>) but meaning-change rewrites consume budget.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Interpretive Summary}

PlenumHub does not merely track semantic edits—it constrains them to a coherent algebra of meaning evolution in which:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{center}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Meaning change is the only resource that costs,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
re-arranging meaning is free,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
and all valid histories collapse to one canonical diagram.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{center}

This places semantic governance in the same mathematical regime as quantum circuit coherence and type-theoretic normalization.

</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
