01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-latex"><span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{A4. Traced Structure: Feedback, Provenance, and Self-Reference}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:trace}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

To model recursion, modality feedback, and semantic self-reference, the SpherePOP category
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbf</span></span><span>{Sph}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is extended from a symmetric monoidal category (SMC) to a
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{symmetric traced monoidal category} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{Joyal1996,Selinger2010}.
This equips PlenumHub with principled mechanisms for:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Recirculating semantic outputs as new inputs (e.g., self-revision, autocomplete loops)
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Provenance tracing without breaking rewrites
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Cycle-aware merge resolution
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Bounded semantic recursion under entropy limits
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Trace Operator Definition}

For any morphism:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
f : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> U </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> U
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
the trace operator closes the </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-channel as a feedback loop:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f) : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> Y
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Diagrammatically:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f)
=
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}[baseline=(c)]
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> (c) at (0,0) {};
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;] (-1,0.4) -- (0,0.4);
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span> (0,0.4) arc (90:-90:0.4);
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\draw</span></span><span>[-&gt;] (0,-0.4) -- (1,-0.4);
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span> at (-0.2,0) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\node</span></span><span>[font=</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\small</span></span><span>] at (0.6,0.6) {</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>};
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzpicture}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

Feedback is permitted only if entropy remains finite and non-escalating.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Trace Axioms and Semantic Guarantees}

Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>I</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the monoidal unit and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> the symmetry map. The trace satisfies:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Vanishing I}:
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>I(f) = f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Vanishing II}:
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{U</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> V}(f) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>V(f))</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Yanking}:
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{U,U}) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Superposing}:
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Sliding}:
  </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U((X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> h);f) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f;(Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> h))</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

These ensure that feedback semantics are invariant under re-parenthesization, rewiring, and modular boundary changes.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Entropy Discipline on Feedback}

Because trace creates cycles, we require entropy boundedness:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>U(f)) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\log</span></span><span>(1 + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\dim</span></span><span> U)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This ensures:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Feedback cannot create unbounded semantic amplification
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Self-rewriting loops must converge or dissipate
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Semantic mining (e.g., texture/time crystal generation) always carries a well-defined cost
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{lemma}[Cycle Entropy Bound]
Any feedback loop that strictly increases entropy at each pass is forbidden.
Formally, if
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) &gt; 0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{and}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\exists</span></span><span> k: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span> k}) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}(f)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is rejected at type-check time.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{lemma}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Provenance as a Traced Monad}

Feedback-enabled semantic logs form a traced Kleisli category:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
f : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}(Y </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> H)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

where:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>Y</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = semantic output
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = edit history (provenance trace)
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> = plenum distribution over alternatives
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

Tracing over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>H</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> closes the history loop:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>H(f) : X </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{P}(Y)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

This yields:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> *History-aware merging without linear ancestry*
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> *Reproducible alternate histories*
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> *Self-correcting documents that retain epistemic source paths*
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Semantic Crystal Minting via Feedback}

Texture-crystal and time-crystal tokens emerge as *stable traced fixed points*:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span> = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\operatorname</span></span><span>{Tr}(f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{id})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

with stability condition:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ast</span></span><span>) = 0, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>(f) / </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\partial</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> 0
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

These fixed points correspond to:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Stabilized multimodal knowledge artifacts
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Microcurrency tokens backed by semantic convergence
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Canonical high-coherence media quines
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

No mining by brute iteration is permitted unless entropy decreases.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsubsection</span></span><span>{Interpretive Summary}

The trace structure transforms PlenumHub from a *graph of meaning changes* into a
*semantic system capable of controlled self-reference*:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{quote}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Users do not merely edit meaning.  
They close feedback loops that evolve meaning,  
and the system pays them in coherence, not computation.}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{quote}

This reframes version control, authorship, and currency as consequences of
semantic fixed points rather than linear append or proof-of-work.

</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
