</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{abstract}
PlenumHub replaces linear version control with a compositional semantic substrate in which knowledge units ("spheres") live in a traced symmetric monoidal category equipped with entropy-typed rewrite rules. We synthesize the core algebraic structure, define SpherePOP calculus with full typing judgment, provide entropy-bounded merge semantics, and derive principled feedback operators enabling provenance-preserving self-reference. Texture and time crystals emerge as entropy-stable traced fixed points, forming a semantic microcurrency grounded in irreversibility bounds rather than external consensus.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{abstract}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Axiomatic Semantic Substrate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:A1}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Spheres]
A sphere </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a modality-indexed semantic unit labeled with entropy </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\entropy</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathbb</span></span><span>{R}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ge</span></span><span> 0}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Modalities include text, vision, audio, code, proofs, or embeddings.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Primitive Operators]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pop</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ldots</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\merge</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\close</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span>: </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{aligned}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Entropy Typing]
Every judgment carries entropy bounds:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sphere</span></span><span> : </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{M} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> [</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\entropy</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\leq</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
Type checking fails if a rule would violate </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\entropy</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{definition}

