</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Operational Semantics and Rewrite System}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\label</span></span><span>{sec:operational-semantics}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

This section presents the executable semantics of the PlenumHub substrate. We give a full small-step and big-step semantics for SpherePOP, define error and mediation states, specify the rule-application machine, and state key metatheorems guaranteeing determinism (up to entropy-guarded nondeterminism), type safety, and entropy accounting.

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Semantic States and Configurations}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{definition}[Machine configuration]
A runtime configuration is a tuple:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C} = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the sphere store (a finite map </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>I </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mapsto</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>),
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the current active sphere,
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the rule trace (a stack or log of applied rules),
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the crystal account state </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{TC}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{TiC})</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
