</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Entropy Violation.}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>') &gt; E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span>}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Error}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{EntropyOverflow}, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span>)}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textsc</span></span><span>{S-Entropy-Err})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Modality Fault.}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{r : a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> b </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> M</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>(a) = </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\varnothing</span></span><span>}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Error}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{MissingModality}(a),</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span>)}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textsc</span></span><span>{S-Modality-Err})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Crystal Exhaustion.}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{TiC} &lt; </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{cost}}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\kappa</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Error}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{OutOfCrystals},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\chi</span></span><span>)}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textsc</span></span><span>{S-Crystal-Err})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Big-Step Evaluation}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

Evaluation iterates small steps until a terminal form:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\quad</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>1 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textsc</span></span><span>{E-Trans})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qquad</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\frac</span></span><span>{}{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\;</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textsc</span></span><span>{E-Term})
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Determinism and Admissible Nondeterminism}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

Unlike pure functional calculi, PlenumHub intentionally admits bounded nondeterminism during mediation search:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Quasi-determinism]
If mediation does not occur, evaluation is deterministic.  
If mediation occurs, all admissible outcomes lie within </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>C </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cdot</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> in semantic divergence (Sec.~</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ref</span></span><span>{sec:semantic-entropy}).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Progress and Preservation}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Preservation]
If </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is well-typed and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span>'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is well-typed.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Progress]
A well-typed non-terminal configuration is never stuck: either it steps or becomes an admissible error state.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Entropy Accounting Invariant}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{theorem}[Entropy Budget Soundness]
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0 </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Downarrow</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span>{C}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Then the final entropy satisfies:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>f) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\le</span></span><span> E(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sigma</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>0) + </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\sum</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{r </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rho</span></span><span>} </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\epsilon</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>r + m</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\delta</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
where </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>m</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is the number of mediated merges.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{theorem}

</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Operational Takeaways}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ============================================================</span></span><span>

The rewrite system guarantees:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No unbounded entropy growth,
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No untyped rule application,
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No merge without crystal stake and entropy clearance,
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> No modality omission after closure,
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Deterministic execution except for bounded mediation search.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

This concludes the operational semantics of PlenumHub’s SpherePOP machine.
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
