<p data-start="320" data-end="355">Two quick notes before the content:</p>
<ul data-start="356" data-end="1063">
<li data-start="356" data-end="850">
<p data-start="358" data-end="850">I wrote the Lean code in a style compatible with Lean 4 / mathlib4 idioms. I could not run or check it here, so a few lemmas/theorems are left with <code data-start="506" data-end="513">sorry</code> where a full mechanized proof would be long; I marked those clearly so you can iterate with your Lean toolchain. The definitions and relation encodings are complete and intended to be directly loadable into a Lean 4 project; they aim to make proving the stated theorems straightforward with standard tactics and the appropriate imports.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="851" data-end="1063">
<p data-start="853" data-end="1063">The LaTeX section E follows your requested structure (time complexity, approximation algorithms, parallel/distributed algorithms) with theorems and algorithm sketches. Paste it after Section D in your document.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1065" data-end="1068">
