This Stage 2 snapshot implements the Type Theory + Entropy Effects workstream for PlenumHub:
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Expanded Section B (Type theory + entropy effects) drafted for LaTeX.
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> A Lean formalization skeleton with basic definitions and a few proved lemmas.
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> A small Python reference implementation: Sphere / Rule / Merge, plus minimal interpreter and tests.
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> A TikZ architecture diagram (standalone .tex) for insertion into the paper.
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> A semantic entropy Section C draft and complexity starter notes (Section E).

This directory is intended as a working starting point for formal verification, experimental evaluation, and full-paper integration.

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## How to run tests (Python)</span></span><span>
<span class="hljs-code">```bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt   # if you add one; dependencies: pytest
pytest src/python/tests
</span></span></span></code></div></div></pre>
<h2 data-start="2603" data-end="2632">How to run Lean (informal)</h2>
<p data-start="2633" data-end="2817">Open <code data-start="2638" data-end="2659">lean/plenumhub.lean</code> in your local Lean + mathlib environment (Lean 3 or Lean 4; the file is a conservative Lean 3/4-compatible skeleton). Use <code data-start="2782" data-end="2788">lake</code> or <code data-start="2792" data-end="2801">leanpkg</code> as appropriate.</p>
<h2 data-start="2819" data-end="2830">Contents</h2>
<p data-start="2831" data-end="2869">See repository tree in this directory.</p>
