# Future Directions (Stage </span><span><span class="hljs-number">2</span></span><span> → Stage </span><span><span class="hljs-number">3</span></span><span>)

This file captures proposed next steps </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> concrete experiments </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">to</span></span><span> pursue </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">after</span></span><span> Stage </span><span><span class="hljs-number">2.</span></span><span>

## Formal/Proof </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Work</span></span><span>
- Port `plenumhub.lean` </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">to</span></span><span> a fully mathlib-compliant project.
- Prove </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Type</span></span><span> Preservation, Progress, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> Entropy Monotonicity </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> the typed calculus.

## Implementation
- </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">Add</span></span><span> a deterministic proof-certificate format (</span><span><span class="hljs-type">JSON</span></span><span>-LD) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> signature </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">schema</span></span><span>.
- Implement a pushout-style structural merger </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> small </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">schema</span></span><span> languages (</span><span><span class="hljs-type">JSON</span></span><span>-</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">like</span></span><span>).
- Build a sandboxed WASM plugin host </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> permitted modality transducers.

## Experiments
- Microbenchmarks </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> `pop`, `merge`, </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">and</span></span><span> `</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">close</span></span><span>` </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">over</span></span><span> small synthetic spheres.
- Ablation: remove entropy guard, measure semantic drift metrics </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">on</span></span><span> toy corpus.

## Socio-technical
- Design incentive simulations </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span></span><span> Texture / </span><span><span class="hljs-type">Time</span></span><span> Crystals (TC / TiC).
- Small </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">user</span></span><span> study: editing tasks </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">with</span></span><span> SpherePOP vs Git.

(Use this file </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">as</span></span><span> a living plan; Stage </span><span><span class="hljs-number">3</span></span><span> will </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">execute</span></span><span> priority items </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> here.)
