</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Pop (single rule application): O(1) metadata updates + cost of transducer (modality dependent)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Pop (rule chain length r): O(r) overhead + sum of transducer costs
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Merge (naive structural): linear in content size; semantic pushout and mediation is combinatorial and can be NP-hard in schema alignment
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> Mediation search: heuristics (beam search, greedy local edits) recommended; A* with admissible heuristic (entropy lower bound) works for small search spaces
