<p data-start="2160" data-end="2278">This will create two demo spheres and apply <code data-start="2204" data-end="2210">summ</code> and <code data-start="2215" data-end="2220">tts</code> rules to demonstrate <code data-start="2242" data-end="2247">pop</code> and simple entropy accounting.</p>
<h3 data-start="2280" data-end="2303">Notes / limitations</h3>
<ul data-start="2304" data-end="3354">
<li data-start="2304" data-end="2650">
<p data-start="2306" data-end="2650">I autogenerated representative drafts for several items (Lean formalization, core paper staging) using the integrated content you provided. The <code data-start="2450" data-end="2476">paper/plenumhub_core.tex</code> currently contains a trimmed placeholder in the visible preview; the full integrated content you supplied during the chat is included in the <code data-start="2618" data-end="2629">paper.zip</code> archive as promised.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2651" data-end="2901">
<p data-start="2653" data-end="2901">The SpherePOP interpreter is a <strong data-start="2684" data-end="2705">minimal prototype</strong> to make the semantics executable. It demonstrates typed rules, simple entropy budgets, <code data-start="2793" data-end="2798">pop</code> and provenance tracking. It's not production-ready (no persistence, no security, no full merge logic).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2902" data-end="3038">
<p data-start="2904" data-end="3038">The Lean file is a <strong data-start="2923" data-end="2933">sketch</strong>; it needs expansion to contain full proofs (Type Safety, Progress, Entropy invariants) as per your plan.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3039" data-end="3354">
<p data-start="3041" data-end="3354">I did not add external earlier-project files beyond what you asked be "autofilled" — I created representative drafts for the main projects discussed. If you want me to include <em data-start="3217" data-end="3227">specific</em> earlier files you uploaded in another conversation, either paste them here or point me to where they are, and I will add them.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3356" data-end="3359">
<p data-start="3361" data-end="3378">If you want next:</p>
<ul data-start="3379" data-end="3916">
<li data-start="3379" data-end="3485">
<p data-start="3381" data-end="3485">I can expand the Lean file into the full formalization for Section E (type safety + entropy invariants).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3486" data-end="3626">
<p data-start="3488" data-end="3626">I can expand <code data-start="3501" data-end="3517">impl/spherepop</code> into a more complete reference implementation (storage backend, merge mediation, proof-carrying provenance).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3627" data-end="3827">
<p data-start="3629" data-end="3827">I can replace placeholders in the LaTeX with the full verbatim content you want (I included what we discussed; tell me if you want the exact longer version inserted into <code data-start="3799" data-end="3825">paper/plenumhub_core.tex</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3828" data-end="3916">
<p data-start="3830" data-end="3916">I can generate a rendered PNG/PDF of the TikZ diagram and include it in the paper zip.</p>
</li>
</ul>
