/path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-python"><span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> reportlab.platypus </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> SimpleDocTemplate, Paragraph, Spacer, PageBreak
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> reportlab.lib.styles </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> getSampleStyleSheet
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">from</span></span><span> reportlab.lib.units </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">import</span></span><span> inch

styles = getSampleStyleSheet()
doc = SimpleDocTemplate(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"/mnt/data/PlenumHub_Arxiv.pdf"</span></span><span>, pagesize=(</span><span><span class="hljs-number">8.5</span></span><span>*inch,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">11</span></span><span>*inch))

story = []

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">h</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">t</span></span><span>):
    story.append(Paragraph(t, styles[</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Heading1"</span></span><span>]))
    story.append(Spacer(</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.2</span></span><span>*inch))
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">h2</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">t</span></span><span>):
    story.append(Paragraph(t, styles[</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Heading2"</span></span><span>]))
    story.append(Spacer(</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.15</span></span><span>*inch))
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-title function_">p</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-params">t</span></span><span>):
    story.append(Paragraph(t, styles[</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"BodyText"</span></span><span>]))
    story.append(Spacer(</span><span><span class="hljs-number">1</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-number">0.12</span></span><span>*inch))

h(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"PlenumHub: A Semantic Compute Substrate for Coherent Collective Intelligence"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Current collaboration substrates encode textual change rather than meaningful structure. "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"PlenumHub introduces knowledge as typed multimodal state vectors evolving under entropy constraints, algebraic composition laws, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"and Media-Quine closure. We formalize the SpherePOP calculus, a thermodynamic merge model, and a proof-carrying rewrite substrate "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"that replaces diffs with typed rule homotopies. A crystal-based microeconomy bounds disorder and governs semantic mediation, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"yielding a verifiable environment for collaborative intelligence with provable invariants, interpretable evolution, and cross-modal completeness."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"1. Introduction &amp; Problem Statement"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Collaboration systems today fall into two primary paradigms: syntactic version control (e.g., Git) and engagement-optimized feeds. "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Neither encodes meaning as a structured, conserved, computable quantity. This leads to semantic drift, orphaned modalities, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"broken provenance, and unprincipled merge conflicts."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"2. Knowledge as Thermodynamic State"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"A semantic sphere is defined as σ = (I, T, M, E, S) where I is identity, T modality types, M modality payloads, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"E semantic entropy, and S a provenance DAG of rule applications. Merge σₐ ⊕ σᵦ is valid only if "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"E(σₘ) ≤ max(Eₐ, Eᵦ) + ε_merge, bounding disorder growth at the substrate level."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"3. SpherePOP Calculus of Meaning"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Transformations are typed rewrite rules r : Mₐ → Mᵦ with entropy budget εᵣ. Rule chains compose as R = r₁;r₂;...;rₙ, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"and execute if each step respects modality typing and entropy budgets. This yields type safety, entropy safety, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"compositional homotopy of meaning, and deterministic replay of semantic histories."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"4. Media-Quine Closure"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Semantic completeness requires Q(σ) = σ iff ∀k∈T, M(k) ≠ ∅. This enforces cross-modal closure, ensuring text⇄audio⇄proof⇄code⇄embedding "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"can be regenerated without external supplementation."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"5. Crystals: Pricing Semantic Disorder"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Texture Crystals (TC) pay for edits and modality synthesis. Time Crystals (TiC) pay for mediation, history anchoring, and merge arbitration. "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"This creates a thermodynamic economy where disorder carries real cost and coherence is rewarded."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"6. Formal Guarantees"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"PlenumHub provides type preservation, progress, entropy-bounded merges, deterministic replay, and bounded confluence under mediation. "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"These are mechanized in Lean and implemented in the reference interpreter."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"7. System Architecture"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Application Layer → Sphere Graph UI; Consensus Layer → Crystal-weighted merge mediation; Core VM → SpherePOP interpreter; "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"State Store → Provenance DAG + entropy ledger; Economics → TC/TiC staking and validation."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"8. Future Work"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"Directions include A* merge mediation, Lean-verified proof traces, persistent homology over sphere lattices, equivariant neural rule proposal, "</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"and quantum-inspired merge search."</span></span><span>)

h2(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"References"</span></span><span>)
p(</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"[1] Landauer, 'Irreversibility and heat generation in the computing process', IBM J. Res. Dev., 1961.&lt;br/&gt;"</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"[2] Mac Lane, 'Categories for the Working Mathematician', Springer, 1998."</span></span><span>)

doc.build(story)

</span><span><span class="hljs-string">"/mnt/data/PlenumHub_Arxiv.pdf"</span></span><span>
