<p data-start="62" data-end="362">Before I generate the <strong data-start="84" data-end="121">full ArXiv-style LaTeX manuscript</strong> (including all theorems, proofs, higher-categorical coherence, entropy-lax monoidality, crystal valuation invariants, and the universal property), I need <strong data-start="276" data-end="306">one final precision choice</strong> that will fix the foundations of the category we build:</p>
<hr data-start="364" data-end="367">
<h2 data-start="369" data-end="432">The core ambient framework for \(\mathcal{P}\) (PlenumHub)</h2>
<p data-start="434" data-end="474">Which of these best matches your intent?</p>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="476" data-end="1158" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="476" data-end="517"><tr data-start="476" data-end="517"><th data-start="476" data-end="485" data-col-size="sm">Choice</th><th data-start="485" data-end="502" data-col-size="sm">Formal setting</th><th data-start="502" data-end="517" data-col-size="lg">Consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="532" data-end="1158"><tr data-start="532" data-end="688"><td data-start="532" data-end="540" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="534" data-end="539">1</strong></td><td data-start="540" data-end="577" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="542" data-end="576">Quasi-categories (Joyal/Lurie)</strong></td><td data-start="577" data-end="688" data-col-size="lg">Best for ∞-categorical universal properties, homotopy limits, adjunctions, and coherent monoidal structures</td></tr><tr data-start="689" data-end="812"><td data-start="689" data-end="697" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="691" data-end="696">2</strong></td><td data-start="697" data-end="723" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="699" data-end="722">Segal spaces (Rezk)</strong></td><td data-start="723" data-end="812" data-col-size="lg">Best if you want a model closer to simplicial sheaves and “spaces of commits/objects”</td></tr><tr data-start="813" data-end="943"><td data-start="813" data-end="821" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="815" data-end="820">3</strong></td><td data-start="821" data-end="858" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="823" data-end="857">Combinatorial model categories</strong></td><td data-start="858" data-end="943" data-col-size="lg">Best if you want explicit cofibration/fibration machinery and Quillen adjunctions</td></tr><tr data-start="944" data-end="1047"><td data-start="944" data-end="952" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="946" data-end="951">4</strong></td><td data-start="952" data-end="968" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="954" data-end="967">∞-operads</strong></td><td data-start="968" data-end="1047" data-col-size="lg">Best if PlenumHub’s composition is fundamentally <em data-start="1019" data-end="1026">n-ary</em> rather than binary</td></tr><tr data-start="1048" data-end="1158"><td data-start="1048" data-end="1056" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1050" data-end="1055">5</strong></td><td data-start="1056" data-end="1079" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1058" data-end="1078">(∞,2)-categories</strong></td><td data-start="1079" data-end="1158" data-col-size="lg">Best if merge morphisms between morphisms (meta-merges) must be first-class</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 48.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.