<hr data-start="1160" data-end="1163">
<h3 data-start="1165" data-end="1195">Notes to guide the choice:</h3>
<ul data-start="1197" data-end="1590">
<li data-start="1197" data-end="1270">
<p data-start="1199" data-end="1270"><strong data-start="1199" data-end="1270">If PlenumHub is “Git but coherent up to homotopy at all levels” → 1</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1271" data-end="1341">
<p data-start="1273" data-end="1341"><strong data-start="1273" data-end="1341">If PlenumHub is “a space of semantic states with continuity” → 2</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1342" data-end="1433">
<p data-start="1344" data-end="1433"><strong data-start="1344" data-end="1433">If PlenumHub is “a system with rewrite homotopies and explicit weak equivalences” → 3</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1434" data-end="1508">
<p data-start="1436" data-end="1508"><strong data-start="1436" data-end="1508">If PlenumHub is “dependent on n-way semantic merges, not binary” → 4</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1509" data-end="1590">
<p data-start="1511" data-end="1590"><strong data-start="1511" data-end="1586">If conflict resolution, proofs about merges, and audits are 2-morphisms</strong> → 5</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1592" data-end="1595">
<h3 data-start="1597" data-end="1667">I suspect the best match might be <strong data-start="1635" data-end="1645">1 or 5</strong>, but you get to pick.</h3>
<p data-start="1669" data-end="1680">Reply with:</p>
<p data-start="1682" data-end="1702"><strong data-start="1682" data-end="1702">1, 2, 3, 4, or 5</strong></p>
<p data-start="1704" data-end="1724">and I will generate:</p>
<ul data-start="1726" data-end="1930">
<li data-start="1726" data-end="1750">
<p data-start="1728" data-end="1750">the full LaTeX article</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1751" data-end="1783">
<p data-start="1753" data-end="1783">the theorem and proof sections</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1784" data-end="1806">
<p data-start="1786" data-end="1806">all diagrams in TikZ</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1807" data-end="1840">
<p data-start="1809" data-end="1840">references in <code data-start="1823" data-end="1840">thebibliography</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1841" data-end="1867">
<p data-start="1843" data-end="1867">correct ArXiv formatting</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1868" data-end="1885">
<p data-start="1870" data-end="1885">no placeholders</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1886" data-end="1904">
<p data-start="1888" data-end="1904">no informal text</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1905" data-end="1930">
