</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\section</span></span><span>{Foundations and Conventions}

We work in the model of </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{quasi-categories} (simplicial sets satisfying inner horn filling),
as developed in </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{HTT}. Unless stated otherwise, ``</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-category'' means ``quasi-category.''

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Core References and Standing Results}

We invoke the following standard results without reproof:

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Joyal model structure on simplicial sets:} 
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Thm.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.2.5.1]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Yoneda embedding and Yoneda lemma for quasi-categories:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Prop.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>5.1.3.1, Cor.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>5.1.5.4]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Limits, colimits, and (co)initial objects in slice </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Def.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>4.1.1.1, Prop.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>4.1.3.1, Cor.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>4.1.3.5]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Straightening–unstraightening equivalence:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Thm.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>3.2.0.1]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Right and left fibrations classified by presheaves:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Cor.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.2.1.2, Thm.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.2.5.1]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{CoCartesian fibrations classify functors to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Cat}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Cor.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>3.2.2.13]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Adjoint functor theorem for presentable </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Cor.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>5.5.2.9, 5.5.2.11]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Presentable </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories are closed under localization:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Prop.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>5.5.4.15]{HTT}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Symmetric monoidal </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories via coCartesian fibrations over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Fin}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>*</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Def.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.0.0.7, Prop.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.4.2.5]{HA}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-Operads and algebras over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-operads:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Def.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>1.1.2.2, 2.1.1.1, 2.2.1.1]{HA}.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textbf</span></span><span>{Lax monoidal functors modeled via operadic maps:}
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>[Rem.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.4.2.6, Def.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ </span></span><span>2.4.3.1]{HA}.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\subsection</span></span><span>{Conventions}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{enumerate}
    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Cat}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> denotes the </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-category of small </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories 
          (equivalently, the quasi-category of quasi-categories).

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Mapping objects are simplicial sets, written
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Map}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> C}(x,y) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\in</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{sSet},
          </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
          whose connectedness and contractibility determine universal properties.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Limits and colimits are defined by initial and final objects in slice </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories
          </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{/p}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> C</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>{p/}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Parameterized histories and state bundles are modeled as coCartesian fibrations
          </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>p</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\colon</span></span><span> X</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> S</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and identified with functors </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>S</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Cat}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> via straightening.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> When monoidal structure is required, we work in the setting of symmetric monoidal 
          </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-categories </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cite</span></span><span>{HA}, encoded as coCartesian fibrations over </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Fin}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>*</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

    </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Higher ``merge-of-merge'' reasoning is carried out internally in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Cat}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, 
          providing the required </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\infty</span></span><span>,2)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> structure without leaving the quasi-categorical model.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{enumerate}
</span><span><span class="hljs-comment">% ===========================================================================</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
