<p data-start="1056" data-end="1157">All four are valid; all give contractible spaces, but they differ in how the rest of the paper flows.</p>
<h3 data-start="1159" data-end="1191">Recommendation quick summary</h3>
<ul data-start="1192" data-end="1479">
<li data-start="1192" data-end="1256">
<p data-start="1194" data-end="1256"><strong data-start="1194" data-end="1201">1 →</strong> most standard “colimit-of-branches” Git-like semantics</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1257" data-end="1321">
<p data-start="1259" data-end="1321"><strong data-start="1259" data-end="1266">2 →</strong> strongest universal property if merges are <em data-start="1310" data-end="1321">receivers</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1322" data-end="1366">
<p data-start="1324" data-end="1366"><strong data-start="1324" data-end="1331">3 →</strong> strongest if merges are <em data-start="1356" data-end="1366">emitters</em></p>
</li>
<li data-start="1367" data-end="1479">
<p data-start="1369" data-end="1479"><strong data-start="1369" data-end="1376">4 →</strong> best if you want branch-merges to behave like transport in a bundle (good for time/entropy fibrations)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="1481" data-end="1523">My suggested default for your project:</h3>
<p data-start="1524" data-end="1573"><strong data-start="1524" data-end="1536">Option 1</strong>, because it integrates cleanly with:</p>
<ul data-start="1574" data-end="1749">
<li data-start="1574" data-end="1611">
<p data-start="1576" data-end="1611">commit DAGs as indexing categories,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1612" data-end="1657">
<p data-start="1614" data-end="1657">entropy bounds as weights on colimit cones,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1658" data-end="1699">
<p data-start="1660" data-end="1699">later symmetry with monoidal envelopes,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1700" data-end="1749">
<p data-start="1702" data-end="1749">and the straightening-based history fibrations.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1751" data-end="1754">
<h3 data-start="1756" data-end="1784">Confirm with one letter:</h3>
<p data-start="1786" data-end="1951"><strong data-start="1786" data-end="1791">1</strong> = colimit cone contractibility (standard merges)<br data-start="1840" data-end="1843">
<strong data-start="1843" data-end="1848">2</strong> = initial object in slice<br data-start="1874" data-end="1877">
<strong data-start="1877" data-end="1882">3</strong> = final object in coslice<br data-start="1908" data-end="1911">
<strong data-start="1911" data-end="1916">4</strong> = cocartesian lift contractibility</p>
<hr data-start="1953" data-end="1956">
<p data-start="1958" data-end="2040">Reply: <strong data-start="1965" data-end="1982">1, 2, 3, or 4</strong><br data-start="1982" data-end="1985">
and I will generate <strong data-start="2005" data-end="2024">Section 3.1–3.6</strong>, starting with:</p>
<ol data-start="2042" data-end="2333">
<li data-start="2042" data-end="2092">
<p data-start="2045" data-end="2092">Formal definition of commit diagrams in <code data-start="2085" data-end="2092">Cat_∞</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2093" data-end="2138">
<p data-start="2096" data-end="2138">Merge cones and indexing simplicial nerves</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2139" data-end="2177">
<p data-start="2142" data-end="2177">Lemmas: cofinality, slice reduction</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2178" data-end="2243">
<p data-start="2181" data-end="2243">Contractibility proof (inner horn filling → Kan core argument)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2244" data-end="2291">
<p data-start="2247" data-end="2291">Corollaries for uniqueness of merge strategy</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2292" data-end="2333">
<p data-start="2295" data-end="2333">TikZ diagram of the universal property</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="2335" data-end="2354" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Ready when you are.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.166