m> notion of a canonical merge, aligns with PlenumHub’s “merge = transport in a history fibration” intuition, and will let us prove uniqueness via <strong data-start="237" data-end="305">contractibility of a maximal Kan subcomplex of cocartesian lifts</strong>.</p>
<p data-start="308" data-end="450">Below is the <strong data-start="321" data-end="398">complete draft of Section 3 (Merge Contractibility via Cocartesian Lifts)</strong> in a mathematical, Lurie-style register, including:</p>
<ol data-start="452" data-end="784">
<li data-start="452" data-end="478">
<p data-start="455" data-end="478">Formal setup in <code data-start="471" data-end="478">Cat_∞</code></p>
</li>
<li data-start="479" data-end="529">
<p data-start="482" data-end="529">Definition of the PlenumHub history fibration</p>
</li>
<li data-start="530" data-end="597">
<p data-start="533" data-end="597">Definition of canonical merge as cocartesian transport of a span</p>
</li>
<li data-start="598" data-end="618">
<p data-start="601" data-end="618">Theorem statement</p>
</li>
<li data-start="619" data-end="641">
<p data-start="622" data-end="641">5 supporting lemmas</p>
</li>
<li data-start="642" data-end="671">
<p data-start="645" data-end="671">Full contractibility proof</p>
</li>
<li data-start="672" data-end="749">
<p data-start="675" data-end="749">Corollaries (uniqueness, homotopy invariance, stability under base change)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="750" data-end="784">
<p data-start="753" data-end="784">TikZ universal property diagram</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="786" data-end="834">You can drop this directly into your manuscript.</p>
<hr data-start="836" data-end="839">
<h2 data-start="841" data-end="901"><strong data-start="844" data-end="901">3. Canonical Merges as Contractible Cocartesian Lifts</strong></h2>
<h3 data-start="903" data-end="943">3.1. The PlenumHub History Fibration</h3>
<p data-start="945" data-end="1243">Let <strong data-start="949" data-end="964">𝒫 ∈ Cat₍∞₎</strong> denote the PlenumHub quasicategory whose 0-simplices are semantic states and whose 1-simplices are state transitions.<br data-start="1082" data-end="1085">
Let <strong data-start="1089" data-end="1102">𝓗 = N(J)</strong> be the simplicial nerve of the indexing category <strong data-start="1152" data-end="1157">J</strong> of branch histories (typically a finite DAG but not assumed to be downward-closed).</p>
<p data-start="1245" data-end="1310">A <em data-start="1247" data-end="1266">history fibration</em> of PlenumHub is a <strong data-start="1285" data-end="1310">coCartesian fibration</strong></p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="script">H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">p</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.00965em;">H</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1351" data-end="1421">classified (via straightening/unstraightening, HTT §3.2) by a functor:</p>
