<h3 data-start="3283" data-end="3309">3.5. Supporting Lemmas</h3>
<p data-start="3311" data-end="3443"><strong data-start="3311" data-end="3362">Lemma 3.5.1 (Reduction to a Slice Kan Complex).</strong><br data-start="3362" data-end="3365">
Cocartesian lifts over a fixed base arrow form a Kan complex inside the slice:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo separator="true">;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>⊆</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">/</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≃</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cocart}(\sigma; x_1, x_2) \subseteq (\mathcal{E}_{/x_0})^\simeq</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Cocart</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mpunct">;</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⊆</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1052em; vertical-align: -0.3552em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3448em;"><span style="top: -2.5198em; margin-left: -0.0894em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">/</span><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3173em;"><span style="top: -2.357em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.0714em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.5em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size3 size1 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">0</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3552em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.7376em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mrel mtight">≃</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="3524" data-end="3638"><em data-start="3524" data-end="3532">Proof:</em> HTT 2.4.4: cocartesian edges are stable under equivalence and compose uniquely up to contractible choice.</p>
<hr data-start="3640" data-end="3643">
<p data-start="3645" data-end="3810"><strong data-start="3645" data-end="3682">Lemma 3.5.2 (Inner Horn Filling).</strong><br data-start="3682" data-end="3685">
Every inner horn in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cocart}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Cocart</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> extends uniquely up to contractible choice to a 2-simplex in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p data-start="3812" data-end="3888"><em data-start="3812" data-end="3820">Proof:</em> By cocartesian lifting property and Joyal model structure fibrancy.</p>
<hr data-start="3890" data-end="3893">
<p data-start="3895" data-end="4041"><strong data-start="3895" data-end="3940">Lemma 3.5.3 (Uniqueness of Lift Targets).</strong><br data-start="3940" data-end="3943">
Given two cocartesian lifts of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05556em;">γ</span></span></span></span>, their endpoints are equivalent in the fiber over <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">m</span></span></span></span>.</p>
<p data-start="4043" data-end="4113"><em data-start="4043" data-end="4051">Proof:</em> HTT 3.1.2.1 – cocartesian lifts are unique up to equivalence.</p>
<hr data-start="4115" data-end="4118">
<p data-start="4120" data-end="4248"><strong data-start="4120" data-end="4155">Lemma 3.5.4 (Loop Contraction).</strong><br data-start="4155" data-end="4158">
Every loop in the maximal Kan subcomplex of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">o</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cocart}(\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathrm">Cocart</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">σ</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> is null-homotopic.</p>
<p data-start="4250" data-end="4330"><em data-start="4250" data-end="4258">Proof:</em> Follows from 3.5.2 and 3.5.3; loops lift to 2-simplices that fill them.</p>
<hr data-start="4332" data-end="4335">
<p data-start="4337" data-end="4429"><strong data-start="4337" data-end="4368">Lemma 3.5.5 (Connectivity).</strong><br data-start="4368" data-end="4371">
The cocartesian lift space is nonempty and path-connected.</p>
<p data-start="4431" data-end="4552"><em data-start="4431" data-end="4439">Proof:</em> Nonemptiness from existence of cocartesian lifts (p is a coCartesian fibration). Connectedness from Lemma 3.5.4.</p>
<hr data-start="4554" data-end="4557">
<h3 data-start="4559" data-end="4588">3.6. Proof of Theorem 3.4</h3>
<ol data-start="4590" data-end="4780">
<li data-start="4590" data-end="4626">
<p data-start="4593" data-end="4626">By Lemma 3.5.1, the space is Kan.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4627" data-end="4656">
<p data-start="4630" data-end="4656">By 3.5.5, it is connected.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4657" data-end="4707">
<p data-start="4660" data-end="4707">By 3.5.4, all endomorphisms are null-homotopic.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4708" data-end="4780">
<p data-start="4711" data-end="4780">A connected Kan complex with trivial homotopy groups is contractible.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.675em;"></span><span class="mord amsrm">□</span></span></span></span></span>
<hr data-start="4797" data-end="4800">
<h3 data-start="4802" data-end="4823">3.7. Consequences</h3>
<p data-start="4825" data-end="4947"><strong data-start="4825" data-end="4864">Corollary 3.7.1 (Merge Uniqueness).</strong><br data-start="4864" data-end="4867">
Any two canonical merges are equivalent by a contractible space of equivalences.</p>
<p data-start="4949" data-end="5066"><strong data-start="4949" data-end="4990">Corollary 3.7.2 (Homotopy Stability).</strong><br data-start="4990" data-end="4993">
Merge commutes with homotopy reparameterization of histories in the base.</p>
<p data-start="5068" data-end="5201"><strong data-start="5068" data-end="5112">Corollary 3.7.3 (Base-change Stability).</strong><br data-start="5112" data-end="5115">
For any cartesian square of histories, canonical merges pull back to canonical merges.</p>
