<p data-start="5420" data-end="5501">The dotted arrow is the contractibly unique cocartesian lift realizing the merge.</p>
<hr data-start="5503" data-end="5506">
<h3 data-start="5508" data-end="5531">3.9. Interpretation</h3>
<ul data-start="5533" data-end="5849">
<li data-start="5533" data-end="5602">
<p data-start="5535" data-end="5602">Canonical merges in PlenumHub are <strong data-start="5569" data-end="5601">not algorithms or heuristics</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5603" data-end="5674">
<p data-start="5605" data-end="5674">They are <strong data-start="5614" data-end="5673">contractible solutions to a fibrational lifting problem</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5675" data-end="5745">
<p data-start="5677" data-end="5745">Any two merge strategies differ by <strong data-start="5712" data-end="5731">null-homotopies</strong>, not choices.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5746" data-end="5849">
<p data-start="5748" data-end="5849">Conflict resolution algorithms are optimizations that must <strong data-start="5807" data-end="5825">factor through</strong> this contractible core.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="5851" data-end="5854">
<h3 data-start="5856" data-end="5910">3.10. Next Section Preview (you will approve next)</h3>
<p data-start="5912" data-end="5924">We now show:</p>
<blockquote data-start="5926" data-end="6107">
<p data-start="5928" data-end="6107"><strong data-start="5928" data-end="6107">The symmetric monoidal envelope of these merges carries an entropy-lax structure, and the crystal valuation defines a 2-monoidal grading preserved under cocartesian transport.</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<p data-start="6109" data-end="6132">This will let us prove:</p>
<ol data-start="6134" data-end="6272">
<li data-start="6134" data-end="6165">
<p data-start="6137" data-end="6165"><strong data-start="6137" data-end="6165">Merge cost is functorial</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6166" data-end="6215">
<p data-start="6169" data-end="6215"><strong data-start="6169" data-end="6215">Entropy is subadditive under merge tensors</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="6216" data-end="6272">
<p data-start="6219" data-end="6272"><strong data-start="6219" data-end="6272">Crystal microcurrency is a 2-functor into (ℝ₊, +)</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="6274" data-end="6277">
<h3 data-start="6279" data-end="6300">Your next choice:</h3>
<p data-start="6302" data-end="6449">A. Monoidal extension of the merge theorem<br data-start="6344" data-end="6347">
B. Crystal valuation functoriality<br data-start="6381" data-end="6384">
C. Entropy-lax symmetric monoidal structure<br data-start="6427" data-end="6430">
D. All of the above</p>
