mmediately. They form a self-contained expansion of the merge contractibility result into:</p>
<ol data-start="182" data-end="478">
<li data-start="182" data-end="268">
<p data-start="185" data-end="268">a symmetric monoidal (∞-)extension that admits tensoring of histories and merges,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="269" data-end="358">
<p data-start="272" data-end="358">a <code data-start="274" data-end="283">crystal</code> valuation that is a (lax) monoidal functor measuring “crystal cost,” and</p>
</li>
<li data-start="359" data-end="478">
<p data-start="362" data-end="478">an entropy-lax symmetric monoidal structure proving entropy subadditivity and stability under cocartesian transport.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="480" data-end="716">I kept the style consistent with the Lurie/quasicategory register you prefer and included a compact TikZ diagram showing the tensor of histories and cocartesian transports. Paste these sections after your merge-contractibility material.</p>
